# Nexcred frontend — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development, or provide these as
# real environment variables in the actual build/deploy environment. Never
# commit a real .env file — see the repository root .gitignore.
#
# Vite only exposes browser-bundled variables that are prefixed with
# VITE_. This is Vite's build-time mechanism for the same conceptual
# APP_URL described in CLAUDE.md Section 23 and README.md — not a second,
# unrelated configuration system. Backend-only values from that same list
# (API_URL, WEBHOOK_URL, DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, META_APP_ID,
# META_APP_SECRET, MEDIA_STORAGE_PATH, REDIS_URL) belong to the backend's
# own environment configuration once it exists, not this file, and must
# never be prefixed with VITE_ or otherwise exposed to the browser bundle.

# The public URL this Nexcred frontend is served from.
VITE_APP_URL=https://mywhatsapp.nexcred.in
